=== hostages
"Ateula is mine. Twelve when they took her; she'd be seventeen. Clever. Too clever for her own good, her mother said." He stops for a moment. "Iccios is Cobnertos's boy. Big for his age. He wanted to be a smith like his father. And Eponina you know better than I do."

"Rome takes the children of the people it doesn't trust, and raises them Roman, or tries. Some come back speaking Latin and wearing their hair short. Some don't come back."
-> hub

=== tally_back
~ quest hostages read_tally; xp 50
[quest grotto active] ~ quest grotto done done
He takes the stick and turns it over in his big hands as if it might speak. Three notches. Letters burned along the side, small and neat and meaningless.

"Rome's letters." He gives it back. "Sulicena, the headwoman at Vindomagos, west along the river. She trades with everyone. Salt to the sea, wine back. If anyone knows who reads this, she will."
* [latin 45] "Let me look at it again. I know some Latin." -> self_read
* "Vindomagos, then." -> END

=== self_read
~ set tally_read; quest hostages north; known noviodunum; xp 75
You hold the tally to the light. The letters are worn, and Roman soldiers abbreviate everything, but you've seen enough of it. A legion number. A name, Lucius something. And at the end, DEP NOVIOD.

"Noviodunum," you say. "A depot. On the Liger, in Aedui country."
-> report

=== report
~ quest hostages reported; xp 150
"Noviodunum." Vellaunos says it slowly. "Aedui country. The Aedui are Rome's oldest friends in Gaul, and they don't like us much." He goes to the door and looks out at the village: smoke, children, a dog asleep in the mud. "It's a long way. Through the Arverni, who are at war, and the Bituriges, who will be. With winter not yet done."

"Go anyway. Take what you need. And {name}: the assembly is in the spring, when the roads dry. Lucterius will send a man to hear what the Cadurci of Brigodunon decide. Whatever you find, I need to know it before then. If you're not back, they'll decide without you, and I know which way."
* "I'll be back before the spring." -> END

=== pardon
"Dubnacos." He says the name like something he found in his food. "He killed Senovir's son over a cow, three winters ago. Seven winters' exile, that was the judgment, and Senovir thinks it was too soft."

"And now he steals from the gods' shrine and wants to come home for it. That isn't mine to forgive. The druids judge what's taken from the gods, and the judgment is death." He shakes his head. "Give me a reason. A good one."
* [speech 45] "Brigodunon is about to need every man who can hold a sword. He's one. Exile doesn't make him any less ours." -> pardon_yes
* [honor >= 15] "Let him come home on my word. If he breaks the peace, the shame is mine." -> pardon_oath
* [PRE 7] "That tally is the only thread to Ateula. What's a cow against your daughter?" -> pardon_yes
* "You're right. Forget I asked." -> hub

=== pardon_oath
~ set pardon_oath
"On your word." He looks at you a long time. "Then it's your word. I'll hold you to it, and so will Senovir."
-> pardon_yes

=== pardon_yes
~ set pardon_granted; quest grotto pardon_granted; xp 50
[!flag pardon_oath] He's quiet a long time. "Damn you. Yes. You're right, and I hate it."
"Tell him he can come home. Tell him he'll pay Senovir the blood price in cattle, every head of it, and he'll sleep outside the rampart till he has. And tell him if he so much as looks at a cow that isn't his, I'll put him back in that cave myself."
-> hub

=== after
"Still here? Noviodunum isn't getting any closer." But he says it gently.
* "Going." -> END

=== levy
~ set vell_levy
[flag levy_pledged] He hears you out, and then he's quiet so long that the fire needs feeding. "Two children. You promised two children of this village to a man you'd met for the time it takes to cut a notch." He feeds the fire. "Rome has three. Now the king will have two. You'd better be right about him."
[flag levy_self] "You gave yourself instead." He looks at you for a long time. "Then Brigodunon will keep faith, because if it doesn't, it's you they'll come for. That's a heavy thing to hand an old man. Thank you."
[flag levy_lucterius] He laughs, the first time you've heard him laugh. "Through Lucterius. Of course. Lucterius will want it from us in the end, and I'll have a month to think of something. That was well done."
[flag levy_iron] "You paid it in silver." He nods. "Iron I can spare. Iron grows back."
[flag levy_vindomagos] He stops you before you finish. "Vindomagos." His face doesn't move. "Sulicena will know who sent them. Everyone on the Oltis will know. We'll be paying for that in salt and in favors for twenty years." He turns away. "I'd have done the same, maybe. I'd have hated myself for it."
[flag levy_refused] "Nothing?" He rubs his face. "Brave. And when the king's riders come to ask why, I'll be the one talking to them. Next time ask me first."
-> hub

=== vtablets
~ set vell_tablets; xp 50
You tell him what the tablets say. He doesn't interrupt. When you get to the name Dannotalos, he sits down.

"Sold forward. Like grain." He says it to the floor. "We kept faith with Rome for five years so that they'd keep my daughter safe, and they've sold her to an Aeduan for when it's convenient." He looks up, and he isn't old at all for a moment. "Then we owe Rome nothing. Nothing. Tell that to the assembly when the spring comes, and show them those tablets."
-> hub

=== home_all
~ set assembly_ready
[!flag vell_home_seen] -> reunion
"The assembly is waiting on you," he says. "They've been waiting since the snow went."
-> hub

=== reunion
~ set vell_home_seen; honor 5; renown 3; xp 100
Ateula is sitting at his table with her tablets spread out, as if she had never left it, and Vellaunos is standing behind her, not touching her, with his hand an inch from her shoulder and the look of a man who has been given back something he'd already finished grieving for.

"You did it." He has to stop. "All three. Cobnertos hasn't let go of his boy since the gate; he's working one-handed. Your mother..." He shakes his head. "Go and see your mother."

"And then come back. The assembly is waiting on you."
-> hub

=== home_some
~ set assembly_ready
[!flag vell_home_seen] -> reunion_some
"The assembly is waiting on you," he says.
-> hub

=== reunion_some
~ set vell_home_seen; xp 75
[flag epo_out] "Your sister's home. I saw her come up the road with her hair cut like a Roman's, arguing with the carter." He almost smiles.

[flag ateula_stays] He's quiet a long time when you tell him about Ateula. "She stayed." He says it to the fire. "To keep the books." And then, so low you almost don't hear it: "Of course she did."
[flag ateula_stays, item hostage_roll] You give him the tablets she wrote. He can't read them. He holds them anyway, with his thumb in the wax where her stylus went, and then he gives them back. "You'll need these. Not me."
[flag ateula_out, !flag iccios_out] "Ateula's home." He can't say more than that, and doesn't try. "And the smith's boy is still there. Cobnertos hasn't said a word since you came back."

"The assembly is waiting on you. Whatever you tell them, tell them what you saw."
-> hub

=== home_none
~ set assembly_ready
[!flag vell_home_seen] -> reunion_none
"The assembly is waiting on you," he says.
-> hub

=== reunion_none
~ set vell_home_seen
You tell him. Noviodunum, the stakes, the long house, the quartermaster with the cough. Ateula at the table with the rolls. You tell him why you came back without them.

He hears all of it without moving. "Alive," he says, when you've finished. "All three. You saw them." He nods slowly, as if that settled something. "Then they're still worth something to Rome, and we still have something to lose. Tell the assembly. They'll need to hear it."
-> hub

=== assembly
The hall is full: every head of every house in Brigodunon, some from the farms, and Toutorix, Lucterius's man, a hard lean rider with mud to the thigh and the king's gold on his arm. The fire is built up high. Nobody sits.

Toutorix speaks first. Lucterius has sworn the Cadurci to the king. The Ruteni are coming in, and the Nitiobriges, and the Gabali. Every hill fort that holds back is a door left open for Rome. He doesn't threaten. He doesn't need to.

Then old Senovir, who has never forgiven anyone anything. Rome has held our children five years and kept faith in its way. A war is a thing you start, and other people finish.
[flag epo_out] He doesn't look at the hostages who are home, sitting by the wall. Everyone else does.
[!flag epo_out] Everyone looks at the empty place by the wall where three children would sit, if they were here.

Then Vellaunos stands up, and the hall goes quiet. "{name} has been to Noviodunum," he says. "Tell them what you saw."
* [flag vell_tablets] Tell them about the Roman merchant's day book: three children of Brigodunon, bought forward, half paid. -> rise_proof
* [item hostage_roll] Hold up Ateula's roll and read them the right-hand column. -> rise_roll
* [flag pledge_void] "The druids of the Carnutes have judged. Rome broke faith first. Our oath is void." -> rise_druids
* [flag pledge_bound] "The druids of the Carnutes have judged. Rome hasn't broken its word, so we haven't either. We're bound." -> faith_druids
* [speech 40] "Rome keeps our children to sell. I saw the rolls. Whatever we decide, decide it knowing that." -> rise_speech
* [speech 50] "Rome has six legions and grain for a year. I counted it. Keep faith, and keep Brigodunon." -> faith
* [honor >= 25] "I gave my word to bring them back, and I kept it. Rome gave its word too. Let it keep it. We keep ours." -> faith
* [roll speech -15] "War is a thing you start and other people finish. Don't start it." -> faith | rise_lost
* [PRE 6] "Nobody in this hall can make anyone else go to war. Let those who want to ride, ride. The rest stay home." -> split
* [lore 40] "Our grandfathers never voted as one hill on anything. A free people can send its young men to the king and still keep its own fires." -> split
* Say nothing. Let them decide. -> rise_silent

=== rise_proof
~ set brig_rising
The hall is silent while you tell it, and then it isn't. Sold forward, like grain. Half paid. Senovir sits down. Toutorix doesn't smile, but he looks at you the way a man looks at a horse he means to buy.
-> rising

=== rise_roll
~ set brig_rising
You read them the column on the right: a merchant's name, a sum, half paid, half paid, half paid. Nearly a hundred children of a dozen peoples, written in a girl's careful hand. Nobody in the hall can read, and nobody needs to.
-> rising

=== rise_druids
~ set brig_rising
Nobody argues with the Carnutes. Senovir opens his mouth and shuts it again. The oath is void. They're free, and being free, they choose what free men choose in a winter like this one.
-> rising

=== rise_speech
~ set brig_rising
You tell them about the long house and the rolls and the price beside the names. You don't shout. You don't need to. By the time you've finished, the young men are on their feet.
-> rising

=== rise_silent
~ set brig_rising
You say nothing. The hall argues until the fire burns down, and the young men shout, and the old men go quiet one by one. It was always going to go this way. You just didn't push.
-> rising

=== rise_lost
~ set brig_rising
They hear you out. Senovir nods. And then Toutorix stands up and talks about the stakes on the plateau at Gergovia, and Cenabum, and the king's face, and the young men shout you down.
-> rising

=== rising
~ quest hostages done_rising done; set act1_done; renown 5; xp 200
Brigodunon rises. The vote is shouted, not counted. Toutorix clasps Vellaunos's arm and rides out before dark to tell Lucterius, and the smith's fire doesn't go out that night or the next.
~ ending endings/act1.json
* Go. -> END

=== faith_druids
You hold up the bronze wheel, and the hall goes quiet the way a hall does when the gods are mentioned by someone who means it. Toutorix argues anyway; he's young. But Senovir only has to say "the Carnutes" twice, and the old men nod, and the young men look at their feet.
-> faith

=== faith
~ set brig_faith; quest hostages done_faith done; set act1_done; xp 200
It takes all night. In the end it's the young men who are quiet, and Senovir who stands and says it for everyone: Brigodunon keeps faith. It gives the king nothing and Rome no reason. It sits on its hill and waits for the war to go past.

Toutorix leaves without a word. You watch him ride down the hill, and you know what he'll tell Lucterius, and so does everyone else.
~ ending endings/act1.json
* Go. -> END

=== split
~ set brig_split; quest hostages done_split done; set act1_done; xp 200
They argue until the fire goes to ash, and then Vellaunos stands and says what you said, in his own words: let those who want to ride, ride. Forty young men go with Toutorix in the morning. The rest stay, and bank up the rampart, and don't look at each other.

It isn't peace. It isn't war. It's Brigodunon.
~ ending endings/act1.json
* Go. -> END

=== late
~ set brig_rising; set act1_done; quest hostages done_late done
"The assembly met," Vellaunos says. "We couldn't wait any longer. Lucterius's man stood where you're standing and nobody spoke against him, because the one who'd been to Noviodunum wasn't here." He looks old. "Brigodunon rose. It was going to anyway. But you should have been here."
~ ending endings/act1.json
* Go. -> END

=== post
[flag brig_rising] "The young men are drilling in the lower field. Every one of them thinks he'll be home for the harvest." He rubs his face. "There's war everywhere now, and Brigodunon can't spare anyone who knows the roads."
[flag brig_faith] "We kept faith." He says it as if testing a floorboard. "Lucterius hasn't sent anyone. That worries me more than if he had."
[flag brig_split] "Forty of ours are with Lucterius. The rest are here, pretending not to count the days." He looks at the fire. "Half a village at war is still a village at war."
* "Goodbye." -> END
